Trademarks
----------

The GPL grants rights to the code, not to names or logos. "Amnezia",
"AmneziaVPN" and the Amnezia logo belong to their owners; this project uses its
own name and artwork.

Names of third-party components are kept unchanged on purpose, because they
identify software the user actually runs rather than this product:

    AmneziaDNS    an unbound container with Amnezia's configuration, deployed
                  by the user onto their own server
    AmneziaWG     the WireGuard-derived protocol by Amnezia
    OpenVPN, WireGuard, XRay, Cloak, Shadowsocks, IKEv2, unbound, Docker

Renaming any of these would leave users unable to recognise, in this client,
the software they installed themselves.
